This repository redistributes small extracts of third-party data. None of it is
covered by the Apache licence above; each is listed here with its own terms.

1. data/universe/sp500_constituents_2026-09-19.csv
   Company names, sectors, SEC central index keys and index join dates, taken
   from the "List of S&P 500 companies" article on Wikipedia, retrieved
   2026-09-19. Wikipedia text is available under the Creative Commons
   Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence.
   "S&P 500" is a registered trademark of S&P Dow Jones Indices LLC. This
   project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by S&P Dow Jones
   Indices, and the snapshot is a third-party transcription rather than the
   index itself.

2. data/sample/sec/*.parquet
   Extracts from SEC EDGAR: 8-K filing metadata and XBRL company-concept
   facts. United States government works are not subject to copyright.
   Retrieved 2026-09-19 under EDGAR's access policy, which requires a
   descriptive User-Agent and a request rate below ten per second; the client
   in src/esa/sec.py complies with both.

3. data/sample/prices/*.parquet
   Split- and dividend-adjusted daily opening and closing prices for 25
   symbols, retrieved from Yahoo Finance on 2026-09-19 through the yfinance
   package. Yahoo's terms permit personal, non-commercial use. The extract is
   included so that tests and continuous integration can run without network
   access; it is not a redistribution of Yahoo's full dataset and should not
   be relied on for any other purpose.

4. data/sample/factors/ff_daily.parquet
   Daily market, size, value and momentum factor returns and the one-month
   Treasury bill rate, from the Kenneth R. French Data Library at Dartmouth
   College, retrieved 2026-09-19. Provided by Professor French for research
   use, with the request that the source be credited.

